  "note": "Curated by hand for scripts/quality/cite-verify.mjs. ONLY sources and edition years the curator was certain of; omissions are deliberate. A missing year makes a real citation read \"year-mismatch\" (a false alarm a human clears) - a wrong year would make a false one read \"verified\", which is the failure this list exists to prevent. \"family\" entries verify only that the publisher/series exists and publishes in that year, not the specific document. year_range [from, null] = every year from `from` to the current year. v2 (review of PR #113): publisher names live ONLY on family entries — a document entry carries document-specific aliases, so \"<publisher> <invented title>, <year>\" can at most read publisher-only.",
